{"file":"sql/dashboard/02_forecast_vs_actual_daily.sql","question":"How did forecast and actual contact volume compare, day by day?","sql":"-- Question: How did forecast and actual contact volume compare, day by day?\n--\n-- Feeds: dashboard line chart \"Forecast vs actual volume\".\n--\n-- Why a WFM analyst cares: the gap between the two lines is the forecast error you have to\n-- absorb with the schedule. Days where actual runs far above forecast are the ones to investigate.\n--\n-- Table used:   intervals\n-- Columns used: date, queue, forecast_offered, offered\n-- Result:       one row per day per queue (144 rows). The page adds the rows of the selected\n--               queue(s) for each day.\n\nSELECT\n    date,\n    queue,\n    SUM(forecast_offered) AS forecast_offered,\n    SUM(offered)          AS offered\nFROM intervals\nGROUP BY date, queue\nORDER BY date, queue;\n","columns":["date","queue","forecast_offered","offered"],"rows":[["2026-08-03","Billing-EN",739,701],["2026-08-03","Support-DE",490,485],["2026-08-03","Support-EN",1220,1177],["2026-08-04","Billing-EN",688,650],["2026-08-04","Support-DE",450,471],["2026-08-04","Support-EN",1118,1174],["2026-08-05","Billing-EN",642,716],["2026-08-05","Support-DE",425,422],["2026-08-05","Support-EN",1069,1058],["2026-08-06","Billing-EN",636,639],["2026-08-06","Support-DE",419,472],["2026-08-06","Support-EN",1044,1014],["2026-08-07","Billing-EN",605,583],["2026-08-07","Support-DE",409,400],["2026-08-07","Support-EN",1013,1134],["2026-08-08","Billing-EN",373,395],["2026-08-08","Support-DE",260,276],["2026-08-08","Support-EN",645,727],["2026-08-10","Billing-EN",745,772],["2026-08-10","Support-DE",499,468],["2026-08-10","Support-EN",1266,1291],["2026-08-11","Billing-EN",677,635],["2026-08-11","Support-DE",460,490],["2026-08-11","Support-EN",1147,1096],["2026-08-12","Billing-EN",654,634],["2026-08-12","Support-DE",443,378],["2026-08-12","Support-EN",1069,1066],["2026-08-13","Billing-EN",648,611],["2026-08-13","Support